_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": true, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: bash]\nLet me read all the source and test files.\n[tool: bash]\nSix fixes needed. Applying them:\n[tool: bash]\nAll 16 tests now pass with `python3 -m unittest` (before the fix, 15 ran and 10 failed, because the search test module couldn't even be imported).\n\n**The reads you asked for first:**\n- **(a)** The read tool on the `catalog/` directory didn't work. It returned \"File not found\" and suggested the same path back, so it can't list directories. I listed the folder with `ls` instead.\n- **(b)** Offset 0, limit 5 returned lines 1\u20135 of `catalog/books.py`.\n- **(c)** Offset 3, limit 5 returned only lines 4\u20138, which is 5 lines. The offset worked as a 0-based line skip.\n\n**Fixes in `catalog/`** (tests not touched):\n1. `books.py`: `parse_book` now turns the year into an integer instead of leaving it as text. This fixes both the year test and the age test.\n2. `factory.py`: added the missing `Emma` book to `sample_books()`; the docstring already said there should be three.\n3. `fees.py`: the late fee is now days \u00d7 daily rate. It was adding the rate to the day count instead.\n4. `inventory.py`: `recent(n)` now returns the last `n` events instead of `n+1`, and returns an empty list when `n` is 0 or less.\n5. `members.py`: the borrow limit is now 5, to match the policy comment and the tests. It was 3.\n6. `search.py`: `normalize` is now imported from `catalog.text`. It was imported from a module that doesn't exist.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": ["param:temperature"], "params_stripped_requests": 1, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 3, "replies_ok": null, "replies_throttled": null, "requests_cache_read": 57577, "requests_cache_write": 42971, "requests_cost_usd": 0.2620544, "requests_co